(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #108 aliasing probe: in `treating <match> as
 <replacement>`, codegen's `Expr::TreatingAs` arm hands back `replacement`'s
 own computed pointer unchanged when a match fires (no fresh copy) - so
 `append each nm from names treating "" as fallback to cleaned.` can store
 `fallback`'s own pointer into `cleaned`. `fallback`'s later `Set` must not
 free the string `cleaned`'s first element still names.)

a text called fallback is "anon".
a list called names is ["", "bob"].
a list called cleaned is [].
append each nm from names treating "" as fallback to cleaned.
Set fallback to "changed".
Print element 1 of cleaned.
Print element 2 of cleaned.
